# PUF10: 10^16 and more is $FOUT's free format after the "%" (of the magnitude: the sign is lost), where PC-BASIC prints all the digits; $PUFXE drops a leading "0" only when the field is too wide, so 4E-6 fits as .00000, .25 keeps $0.25 and .5 $0.50 (PC-BASIC: %0.00000, $.25, $.50)
